# TweakLens Zero-Memory Cheatsheet

## 1. Start TweakLens (Terminal 1)

```powershell
cd C:\DEV\tweaklens
npm run dev
```

---

## 2. Start Your Project (Terminal 2)

Go to your project folder and run the command for your framework.

### Flutter
```powershell
flutter run -d web-server
```
Copy the `http://localhost:XXXXX` link and paste into TweakLens.

### Next.js / Vite / React
```powershell
npm run dev
```
Copy the local link (e.g. `http://localhost:3000`) and paste into TweakLens.

### Expo / React Native Web
```powershell
npx expo start --web
```
Copy the link and paste into TweakLens.

### Python (Streamlit / Flask)
```powershell
streamlit run app.py   # Streamlit
python app.py          # Flask
```
Copy the link and paste into TweakLens.

