## 5. Exporting to AI

### The prompt includes (automatically)

- Element selectors (`button.subscribe`, `.hero-banner`)
- Component names (`data-tl="ItemCards"`)
- Source file + line (`src/components/.../ItemCards.tsx:97`)
- Current computed styles (before state)
- Your instructions (action, text, color, notes)

### Project rules (toggle ON by default)

The exported prompt includes a **PROJECT RULES** block that tells the AI:
- Follow the repo's AGENTS.md conventions
- Use the existing design system (branding tokens, buttonClass, cardRadius)
- Run typecheck + lint + check-docs after changes
- Make it responsive at all breakpoints

You can uncheck "Include project rules" if you don't need it.

### Where to paste it

| Tool | How |
| :--- | :--- |
| **OpenCode (CLI)** | Paste directly in chat. The AI already has your repo. |
| **Claude / ChatGPT** | Paste the plan + attach the relevant file(s). |
| **Cursor** | Paste in chat. Cursor reads your project files. |
| **Local AI** | Paste only the 1-2 files being edited + the plan. |

