## 6. Device Wall

See **all devices at once** — Mobile, Tablet, Desktop — side by side.

| Button | What it does |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Single** | One device, full interactive control. |
| **Wall** | All 7 devices live side by side, scrollable. |
| **Fit / 1:1** | Toggle between "fit all in view" and "real pixel size". |

### How to use the Wall

1. Click **Wall** in the top-right.
2. All devices load your app simultaneously at real pixel sizes.
3. Switch to **Edit UI Tools** to annotate on any device — annotations are tagged with the device name.
4. Export groups tasks under device headers (e.g. `### 📱 iPhone 14/15 (390×844)`).

### Device presets

| Device | Width × Height | DPR | Touch | Mode |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 📱 iPhone SE | 375 × 667 | 2 | Yes | Mobile |
| 📱 iPhone 14/15 | 390 × 844 | 3 | Yes | Mobile |
| 📱 Pixel 7 | 412 × 915 | 2.6 | Yes | Mobile |
| 📱 iPad (classic) | 768 × 1024 | 2 | Yes | Tablet |
| 📱 iPad 10th | 820 × 1180 | 2 | Yes | Tablet |
| 💻 Laptop | 1280 × 800 | 1 | No | Desktop |
| 🖥️ Desktop HD | 1920 × 1080 | 1 | No | Desktop |

Each device gets real Chrome DevTools Protocol emulation: device metrics, touch mode, User-Agent spoofing, and media features (hover:none, pointer:coarse on mobile). This means CSS `@media` queries fire correctly.

### What it can't do (honest)

TweakLens simulates **screen size and CSS breakpoints** — not a real device. It does NOT simulate:
- Safari / Firefox engines (always Chromium)
- iOS safe-area insets (notch, home bar = 0)
- PWA standalone mode, install, push, offline
- Font rendering differences
- Native apps (only web)

For the final 5%, test on real hardware.

---

## 7. Tips

- **Design at multiple viewports** — switch between devices or use the Wall to see all at once.
- **Source info is automatic** — if the app is React/Next.js, TweakLens reads the component source. If not, you'll get selectors only (still useful).
- **Rules preamble protects you** — the AI won't hardcode colors or break your design system.
- **Annotations are per-device** — an annotation made on Mobile is tagged `📱 iPhone 14/15`. The export groups tasks by device so the AI knows which viewport each change targets.
